Carafe bench: OpenGL typeless image stores and loads through red/blue-swizzled views keep the byte order.
This is the OpenGL side of the Vulkan fix for the same views. NVK describes a BGRA image as A8B8G8R8 with a
B, G, R, A swizzle; a typeless store ignores the swizzle, so NFSU's back-buffer copy came out with red and
blue exchanged. OpenGL has no BGRA image format, so each such view sets a bit in a per-stage uniform and the
GLSL store and load swap the first and third components when the bit is set.
GPL-3.0-or-later, as the files it changes.

